    <h2>Rendering components</h2>

    <p>
        <code>UIRenderer</code>, <code>UITextRenderer</code>,
        <code>SpriteRenderer</code>, and <code>UI3DModelsRenderer</code>
        handle drawing. Text uses Roboto loaded through StbTrueTypeSharp.
        Image loading uses StbImageSharp.
    </p>

    <h2>Inventory and hotbar</h2>

    <p>
        <code>HudInventory</code> owns a TabView, a hotbar SlotGrid,
        a cursor/held slot, and survival/creative inventory pages
        implementing <code>IInventoryLayout</code>. That interface
        groups storage, armor, crafting slots, and the crafting result slot.
    </p>

    <p>
        The inventory slot index space is flat: 0–8 hotbar, 9–35 storage,
        36–39 armor, 40–43 crafting, and 44 crafting result. The creative
        tab view is a scrollable 9 × 6 grid. <code>SlotInteraction</code>
        handles pickup, placement, right-click splitting, and stacking up to 64.
    </p>

    <h2>UI to ECS synchronization</h2>

    <p>
        The player has Inventory and Hotbar components. When a UI slot changes,
        <code>HudInventory.SlotChanged</code> raises a change that
        <code>InventorySystem</code> queues and applies to the ECS on its update.
        In the opposite direction, the system updates HUD slots from component
        state. Resolver delegates map item/block IDs to item meshes and block IDs.
    </p>

    <h2>HUD pieces</h2>

    <p>
        The current HUD includes the nine-slot hotbar, heart display
        (full/half/empty sprites), crosshair, pause menu, inventory pages,
        and death screen. Pressing E toggles inventory and changes game
        state/cursor mode.
    </p>

    <div class="docs-callout docs-callout-info">
